1
00:00:01,069 --> 00:00:02,169
Chapter 26.

2
00:00:03,449 --> 00:00:05,809
Sophie came at seven to dress me.

3
00:00:06,529 --> 00:00:12,069
She was very long indeed in accomplishing her task, so long that Mr. Rochester,

4
00:00:12,650 --> 00:00:17,930
grown, I suppose, impatient of my delay, sent up to ask why I did not come.

5
00:00:18,690 --> 00:00:23,169
She was just fastening my veil, the plain square of blonde, after all,

6
00:00:23,709 --> 00:00:25,190
to my hair with a brooch.

7
00:00:25,750 --> 00:00:28,430
I hurried from under her hands as soon as I could.

8
00:00:29,209 --> 00:00:31,190
Stop, she cried in French.

9
00:00:32,029 --> 00:00:35,410
Look at yourself in the mirror, you have not taken one peep.

10
00:00:36,089 --> 00:00:38,209
So I turned at the door.

11
00:00:39,290 --> 00:00:43,040
I saw a robed and veiled figure, so unlike my usual

12
00:00:43,042 --> 00:00:45,889
self that it seemed almost the image of a stranger.

13
00:00:47,370 --> 00:00:51,370
Jane called a voice, and I hastened down.

14
00:00:52,349 --> 00:00:55,290
I was received at the foot of the stairs by Mr. Rochester.

15
00:00:56,510 --> 00:00:57,790
Lingerah, he said.

16
00:00:58,669 --> 00:01:02,309
My brain is on fire with impatience and you tarry so long.

17
00:01:03,330 --> 00:01:08,849
He took me into the dining-room, surveyed me keenly all over, pronounced me

18
00:01:08,851 --> 00:01:14,449
fair as a lily, and not only the pride of his life, but the desire of his eyes,

19
00:01:15,410 --> 00:01:18,889
and then telling me he would give me but ten minutes to eat some breakfast,

20
00:01:19,750 --> 00:01:20,750
he rang the bell.

21
00:01:21,870 --> 00:01:25,190
One of his lately-hired servants, a footman answered it.

22
00:01:25,830 --> 00:01:27,250
Is John getting the carriage ready?

23
00:01:27,989 --> 00:01:28,989
Yes, sir.

24
00:01:29,470 --> 00:01:30,669
Is the luggage brought down?

25
00:01:31,550 --> 00:01:33,050
They are bringing it down, sir.

26
00:01:34,370 --> 00:01:35,569
Go you to the church.

27
00:01:36,169 --> 00:01:38,930
See if Mr. Wood, the clergyman and the clerk are there.

28
00:01:39,669 --> 00:01:40,669
Return and tell me.

29
00:01:41,970 --> 00:01:46,389
The church, as the reader knows, was but just beyond the gates.

30
00:01:47,430 --> 00:01:48,690
The footman soon returned.

31
00:01:49,889 --> 00:01:53,269
Mr. Wood is in the vestry, sir, putting on his surplus.

32
00:01:54,230 --> 00:01:55,230
And the carriage?

33
00:01:56,129 --> 00:01:57,870
The horses are harnessing.

34
00:01:59,050 --> 00:02:03,730
We shall not want it to go to church, but it must be ready the moment we return.

35
00:02:04,550 --> 00:02:08,589
All the boxes and luggage arranged and strapped on in the coachman in his seat.

36
00:02:09,489 --> 00:02:10,489
Yes, sir.

37
00:02:11,250 --> 00:02:12,250
Jane, are you ready?

38
00:02:13,410 --> 00:02:14,410
I rose.

39
00:02:14,730 --> 00:02:19,629
There were no groomsmen, no bridesmaids, no relatives to wait for or marshal.

40
00:02:20,529 --> 00:02:22,190
None but Mr. Rochester and I.

41
00:02:23,449 --> 00:02:25,970
Mrs. Fairfax stood in the hall as we passed.

42
00:02:27,029 --> 00:02:31,790
I would feign have spoken to her, but my hand was held by a grasp of iron.

43
00:02:32,650 --> 00:02:35,870
I was hurried along by a stride I could hardly follow.

44
00:02:36,470 --> 00:02:40,546
And to look at Mr. Rochester's face was to feel that not

45
00:02:40,546 --> 00:02:43,309
a second of delay would be tolerated for any purpose.

46
00:02:44,370 --> 00:02:48,610
I wonder what other bridegroom ever looked as he did, so bent up to a purpose,

47
00:02:49,110 --> 00:02:52,841
so grimly resolute, or who, under such steadfast

48
00:02:52,841 --> 00:02:56,129
brows, ever revealed such flaming and flashing eyes.

49
00:02:57,809 --> 00:03:00,529
I know not whether the day was fair or foul.

50
00:03:01,169 --> 00:03:05,050
In descending the drive I gazed neither on sky nor earth.

51
00:03:05,669 --> 00:03:11,269
My heart was with my eyes, and both seemed migrated into Mr. Rochester's frame.

52
00:03:12,309 --> 00:03:16,463
I wanted to see the invisible thing on which, as we went

53
00:03:16,463 --> 00:03:20,290
along, he appeared to fasten a glance fierce and fell.

54
00:03:21,230 --> 00:03:25,050
I wanted to feel the thoughts whose force he seemed resting and resisting.

55
00:03:26,250 --> 00:03:28,430
At the churchyard wicked, he stopped.

56
00:03:29,290 --> 00:03:31,250
He discovered I was quite out of breath.

57
00:03:32,709 --> 00:03:35,589
Am I cruel in my love, he said.

58
00:03:36,349 --> 00:03:38,629
Delay an instant, lean on me, Jane.

59
00:03:40,230 --> 00:03:45,349
And now I can recall the picture of the gray old house of God rising calm before

60
00:03:45,351 --> 00:03:50,410
me of a rook wheeling round the steeple of a ruddy morning sky beyond.

61
00:03:51,209 --> 00:03:57,631
I remember something too of the green grave mounds, and I have not forgotten either.

62
00:03:58,150 --> 00:04:01,961
Two figures of strangers straining amongst the low hillocks

63
00:04:01,961 --> 00:04:06,230
and reading the mementos graven on the few mossy headstones.

64
00:04:06,430 --> 00:04:13,169
I noticed them, because as they saw us, they passed round to the back of the

65
00:04:13,171 --> 00:04:16,932
church, and I doubted not they were going to enter

66
00:04:16,934 --> 00:04:20,351
by the side-ile door and witness the ceremony.

67
00:04:21,510 --> 00:04:24,730
By Mr. Rochester, they were not observed.

68
00:04:25,449 --> 00:04:30,150
He was earnestly looking at my face, from which the blood had, I daresay,

69
00:04:30,550 --> 00:04:31,750
momentarily fled.

70
00:04:32,709 --> 00:04:36,709
For I felt my forehead duly and my cheeks and lips cold.

71
00:04:37,569 --> 00:04:43,991
When I rallied, which I soon did, he walked gently with me up the path to the porch.

72
00:04:44,489 --> 00:04:46,870
We entered the quiet and humble temple.

73
00:04:47,730 --> 00:04:52,849
The priest waited in his white surplus at the lowly altar, the clerk beside him.

74
00:04:53,650 --> 00:04:54,690
All was still.

75
00:04:55,830 --> 00:04:59,230
Two shadows only moved in a remote corner.

76
00:05:00,309 --> 00:05:02,110
My conjecture had been correct.

77
00:05:02,930 --> 00:05:07,930
The strangers had slipped in before us, and they now stood by the vault of the

78
00:05:07,930 --> 00:05:14,069
Rochester's, their backs towards us, viewing through the rails the old time

79
00:05:14,071 --> 00:05:19,150
-stained marble tomb, where a kneeling angel guarded the remains of Damodar

80
00:05:19,150 --> 00:05:24,949
Rochester, slain at mastermore in the time of the civil wars and of Elizabeth,

81
00:05:25,650 --> 00:05:26,650
his wife.

82
00:05:27,470 --> 00:05:30,269
Our place was taken at the communion rails.

83
00:05:31,290 --> 00:05:34,709
Hearing a cautious step behind me, I glanced over my shoulder.

84
00:05:35,650 --> 00:05:40,230
One of the strangers, a gentleman evidently, was advancing up the chancel.

85
00:05:41,110 --> 00:05:42,769
The service began.

86
00:05:43,970 --> 00:05:49,169
The explanation of the intent of matrimony was gone through, and then the clergyman

87
00:05:49,171 --> 00:05:52,940
came a step further forward, and bending slightly towards Mr.

88
00:05:53,821 --> 00:05:55,569
Rochester, went on.

89
00:05:56,230 --> 00:06:01,269
I require and charge you both, as you will answer at the dreadful day of

90
00:06:01,271 --> 00:06:05,069
judgment, when the secrets of all hearts shall be disclosed.

91
00:06:05,629 --> 00:06:11,830
That if either of you know any impediment, why you may not lawfully be joined

92
00:06:11,830 --> 00:06:15,610
together in matrimony, you do now confess it.

93
00:06:16,569 --> 00:06:22,129
For be you well assured that so many as are coupled together, otherwise than God's

94
00:06:22,131 --> 00:06:29,430
word doth allow, are not joined together by God, neither is their matrimony lawful.

95
00:06:30,769 --> 00:06:34,029
He paused, as the custom is.

96
00:06:35,209 --> 00:06:39,330
When is the pause after that sentence ever broken

97
00:06:39,330 --> 00:06:42,851
by reply, not perhaps once in a hundred years.

98
00:06:43,529 --> 00:06:47,625
And the clergyman, who had not lifted his eyes from his book,

99
00:06:47,625 --> 00:06:51,190
and had held his breath but for a moment, was proceeding.

100
00:06:51,949 --> 00:06:57,569
His hand was already stretched towards Mr. Rochester, as his lips unclosed to ask,

101
00:06:58,269 --> 00:07:03,269
will thou have this woman for thy wedded wife, when a distinct and near voice said,

102
00:07:04,290 --> 00:07:05,930
the marriage cannot go on.

103
00:07:06,470 --> 00:07:08,849
I declare the existence of an impediment.

104
00:07:09,629 --> 00:07:12,610
The clergyman looked up at the speaker and stood mute.

105
00:07:13,349 --> 00:07:14,389
The clerk did the same.

106
00:07:15,209 --> 00:07:19,629
Mr. Rochester moved slightly, as if an earthquake had rolled under his feet,

107
00:07:20,309 --> 00:07:25,790
taking a firmer footing, and not turning his head or eyes, he said, proceed,

108
00:07:26,769 --> 00:07:32,010
profound silence fell when he had uttered that word, with deep but low intonation.

109
00:07:33,410 --> 00:07:39,750
Presently Mr. Wood said, I cannot proceed without some investigation into what has

110
00:07:39,750 --> 00:07:43,150
been asserted and evidence of its truth or falsehood.

111
00:07:44,069 --> 00:07:48,629
The ceremony is quite broken off, subjoined the voice behind us.

112
00:07:49,529 --> 00:07:52,923
I am in a condition to prove my allegation, an

113
00:07:52,925 --> 00:07:56,129
insuperable impediment to this marriage exists.

114
00:07:57,750 --> 00:08:00,069
Mr. Rochester heard, but he did not.

115
00:08:00,989 --> 00:08:07,290
He stood stubborn and rigid, making no movement but to possess himself of my hand.

116
00:08:07,650 --> 00:08:13,629
What a hot and strong grass he had, and how like quarried marble was his pale,

117
00:08:13,949 --> 00:08:16,150
firm, massive front at this moment.

118
00:08:16,930 --> 00:08:23,391
How his eyes shone, still watchful, and yet wild beneath Mr. Wood seemed at a loss.

119
00:08:23,769 --> 00:08:27,129
What is the nature of the impediment, he asked?

120
00:08:27,930 --> 00:08:30,449
Perhaps it may be got over, explained away?

121
00:08:31,470 --> 00:08:33,089
Hardly was the answer.

122
00:08:34,069 --> 00:08:37,330
I have called it insuperable and I speak advisedly.

123
00:08:38,050 --> 00:08:40,849
The speaker came forward and leaned on the rails.

124
00:08:41,730 --> 00:08:47,991
He continued, uttering each word distinctly, calmly, steadily, but not loudly.

125
00:08:48,470 --> 00:08:51,970
It simply consists in the existence of a previous marriage.

126
00:08:52,629 --> 00:08:54,870
Mr. Rochester has a wife now living.

127
00:08:55,970 --> 00:09:02,211
My nerves vibrated to those low spoken words, as they had never vibrated to thunder.

128
00:09:02,330 --> 00:09:06,930
My blood felt their subtle violence, as it had never felt frost or fire.

129
00:09:07,709 --> 00:09:10,889
But I was collected, and in no danger of swooning.

130
00:09:11,889 --> 00:09:13,510
I looked at Mr. Rochester.

131
00:09:14,650 --> 00:09:15,930
I made him look at me.

132
00:09:16,790 --> 00:09:18,750
His whole face was colourless rock.

133
00:09:19,629 --> 00:09:21,809
His eye was both spark and flint.

134
00:09:22,510 --> 00:09:23,650
He disavowed nothing.

135
00:09:24,330 --> 00:09:29,269
He seemed as if he would defy all things, without speaking, without smiling,

136
00:09:29,510 --> 00:09:32,269
without seeming to recognise in me a human being.

137
00:09:33,069 --> 00:09:36,830
He only twined my waist with his arm and riveted me to his side.

138
00:09:38,269 --> 00:09:39,330
Who are you?

139
00:09:39,989 --> 00:09:41,150
He asked of the intruder.

140
00:09:42,230 --> 00:09:46,269
My name is Briggs, a solicitor of Aar Street, London.

141
00:09:46,949 --> 00:09:49,010
And you would thrust on me a wife?

142
00:09:49,910 --> 00:09:52,603
I would remind you of your lady's existence,

143
00:09:52,605 --> 00:09:56,110
sir, which the law recognises if you do not.

144
00:09:57,309 --> 00:10:00,572
Fave a me with an account of her, with her name,

145
00:10:00,572 --> 00:10:04,769
her parentage, her place of abode, certainly.

146
00:10:06,250 --> 00:10:08,642
Mr. Briggs calmly took a paper from his pocket

147
00:10:08,644 --> 00:10:11,970
and read out in a sort of official nasal voice.

148
00:10:12,769 --> 00:10:19,889
I affirm and can prove that on the 20th of October AD, a date of 15 years back,

149
00:10:20,589 --> 00:10:26,389
Edward Fairfax Rochester, of Thornfield Hall, in the county of Conca, and of

150
00:10:26,391 --> 00:10:31,010
Fendin Manor, in Na'an Shire, England, was married to my sister, Bertha

151
00:10:31,010 --> 00:10:37,089
Antoinette Mason, daughter of Jonas Mason, Merchant, and of Antoinette, his wife,

152
00:10:37,650 --> 00:10:40,910
a Creole, at my church, Spanish town Jamaica.

153
00:10:41,650 --> 00:10:45,050
The record of the marriage will be found in the register of that church.

154
00:10:45,750 --> 00:10:50,510
A copy of it is now in my possession, signed Richard Mason.

155
00:10:51,750 --> 00:10:59,510
That, if a genuine document, may prove I have been married, but it does not prove

156
00:10:59,510 --> 00:11:03,050
that the woman mentioned therein as my wife is still living.

157
00:11:04,430 --> 00:11:07,529
She was living three months ago, returned the lawyer.

158
00:11:08,269 --> 00:11:09,269
How do you know?

159
00:11:09,730 --> 00:11:12,887
I have a witness to the fact, whose testimony,

160
00:11:12,887 --> 00:11:15,930
even you, sir, will scarcely contribute.

161
00:11:16,730 --> 00:11:18,330
Produce him or go to hell.

162
00:11:18,790 --> 00:11:19,949
I will produce him first.

163
00:11:20,309 --> 00:11:21,309
He is on the spot.

164
00:11:21,470 --> 00:11:23,610
Mr. Mason have the goodness to step forward.

165
00:11:25,569 --> 00:11:29,290
Mr. Rochester, on hearing the name, set his teeth.

166
00:11:30,129 --> 00:11:33,930
He experienced two a sort of strong, convulsive quiver.

167
00:11:35,069 --> 00:11:38,141
Near to him, as I was, I felt the spasmodic

168
00:11:38,142 --> 00:11:41,211
movement of fury or despair run through his frame.

169
00:11:42,150 --> 00:11:47,029
The second stranger, who had hitherto lingered in the background, now drew near.

170
00:11:48,169 --> 00:11:50,989
A pale face looked over the solicitor's shoulder.

171
00:11:52,010 --> 00:11:54,089
Yes, it was Mason himself.

172
00:11:55,269 --> 00:11:57,110
Mr. Rochester turned and glared at him.

173
00:11:57,849 --> 00:12:01,209
His eye, as I have often said, was a black eye.

174
00:12:01,211 --> 00:12:08,410
It had now a tawny nay, a bloody light in its gloom, and his face flushed.

175
00:12:09,089 --> 00:12:14,089
Olive cheek and heueless forehead received a glow as from spreading ascending

176
00:12:14,091 --> 00:12:18,470
heartfire, and he stirred, lifted his strong arm.

177
00:12:19,169 --> 00:12:22,391
He could have struck Mason, dashed him on the church

178
00:12:22,391 --> 00:12:25,410
floor, shocked by ruthless blow the breath from his body.

179
00:12:26,430 --> 00:12:30,430
But Mason shrank away and cried faintly, Good God!

180
00:12:31,430 --> 00:12:33,769
Contempt fell cool on Mr. Rochester.

181
00:12:34,589 --> 00:12:37,730
His passion died as if a blight had shriveled it up.

182
00:12:38,410 --> 00:12:41,730
He only asked, What have you to say?

183
00:12:42,790 --> 00:12:45,290
An inaudible reply escaped Mason's white lips.

184
00:12:46,050 --> 00:12:48,750
The devil is in it if you cannot answer distinctly.

185
00:12:49,389 --> 00:12:52,589
I again demand, What have you to say?

186
00:12:53,769 --> 00:12:57,870
Sir, Sir, Interrupted the clergyman.

187
00:12:58,610 --> 00:13:01,129
Do not forget you are in a sacred place.

188
00:13:02,129 --> 00:13:05,250
Then addressing Mason, he inquired gently.

189
00:13:06,309 --> 00:13:10,650
Are you aware, Sir, whether or not this gentleman's wife is still living?

190
00:13:11,569 --> 00:13:14,209
Courage urged the lawyer, Speak out.

191
00:13:15,029 --> 00:13:20,569
She is now living at Thornfield Hall, said Mason, in more articulate tones.

192
00:13:21,529 --> 00:13:22,889
I saw her there last April.

193
00:13:23,250 --> 00:13:24,349
I am her brother.

194
00:13:25,750 --> 00:13:29,730
At Thornfield Hall, ejaculated the clergyman.

195
00:13:30,849 --> 00:13:31,849
Impossible.

196
00:13:32,309 --> 00:13:35,724
I am an old resident in this neighborhood, Sir, and I never heard of a Mrs.

197
00:13:35,726 --> 00:13:37,190
Rochester at Thornfield Hall.

198
00:13:38,610 --> 00:13:42,190
I saw a grim smile, contort Mr. Rochester's lips.

199
00:13:43,169 --> 00:13:45,910
And he muttered, No, by God.

200
00:13:46,730 --> 00:13:51,250
I took care that none should hear of it, or of her under that name.

201
00:13:52,709 --> 00:13:53,709
He mused.

202
00:13:54,370 --> 00:13:56,449
For ten minutes he held counsel with himself.

203
00:13:57,349 --> 00:13:59,709
He formed his resolve and announced it.

204
00:14:00,650 --> 00:14:01,650
Enough.

205
00:14:01,949 --> 00:14:04,750
All shall bolt out at once, like the bullet from the barrel.

206
00:14:05,330 --> 00:14:08,410
Wood, close your book and take off your surplus.

207
00:14:09,269 --> 00:14:10,730
John Green, to the clerk.

208
00:14:11,690 --> 00:14:12,690
Leave the church.

209
00:14:12,849 --> 00:14:14,089
There will be no wedding today.

210
00:14:15,610 --> 00:14:16,629
The man obeyed.

211
00:14:17,589 --> 00:14:20,610
Mr. Rochester continued, hardly and recklessly.

212
00:14:21,650 --> 00:14:23,190
Bigamy is an ugly word.

213
00:14:24,349 --> 00:14:28,830
I meant, however, to be a bigamist, but fate has outmaneuvered me,

214
00:14:29,169 --> 00:14:30,529
or providence has checked me.

215
00:14:31,010 --> 00:14:32,010
Perhaps the last.

216
00:14:32,769 --> 00:14:35,550
I am little better than a devil at this moment.

217
00:14:36,489 --> 00:14:42,029
And, as my pastor there would tell me, deserve no doubt the sternest judgments of

218
00:14:42,031 --> 00:14:45,690
God, even to the quenchless fire and deathless worm.

219
00:14:46,790 --> 00:14:50,110
Gentlemen, my plan is broken up.

220
00:14:50,910 --> 00:14:53,370
What this lawyer and his clients say is true.

221
00:14:53,949 --> 00:14:57,889
I have been married, and the woman to whom I was married lives.

222
00:14:58,930 --> 00:15:02,589
You say you never heard of a Mrs. Rochester at the house up Yonderwood,

223
00:15:03,209 --> 00:15:07,410
but I dare say you have many a time inclined your ear to gossip about the

224
00:15:07,411 --> 00:15:11,029
mysterious lunatic, kept there under watch and ward.

225
00:15:11,889 --> 00:15:15,550
Some have whispered to you that she is my bastard half sister.

226
00:15:16,269 --> 00:15:18,449
Some, my cast off mistress.

227
00:15:19,489 --> 00:15:25,669
I now inform you that she is my wife, whom I married 15 years ago.

228
00:15:26,569 --> 00:15:32,010
Bertha Mason, by name, sister of this resolute personage, who is now,

229
00:15:32,489 --> 00:15:35,250
with his quivering limbs and white cheeks,

230
00:15:35,252 --> 00:15:37,949
showing you what a stout heart men may bear.

231
00:15:38,610 --> 00:15:40,510
Cheer up, Dick, never fear me.

232
00:15:41,050 --> 00:15:43,410
I'd almost as soon strike a woman as you.

233
00:15:44,309 --> 00:15:48,588
Bertha Mason is mad, and she came of a mad family,

234
00:15:48,588 --> 00:15:52,311
idiots and maniacs through three generations.

235
00:15:52,930 --> 00:15:57,322
Her mother, the Creole, was both a mad woman and a

236
00:15:57,322 --> 00:16:00,550
drunkard, as I found out after I had wed the daughter.

237
00:16:01,209 --> 00:16:03,669
For they were silent on family secrets before.

238
00:16:04,589 --> 00:16:09,110
Bertha, like a beautiful child, copied her parent in both points.

239
00:16:09,870 --> 00:16:13,069
I had a charming partner, pure, wise, modest.

240
00:16:13,071 --> 00:16:14,269
You can fancy?

241
00:16:14,690 --> 00:16:15,690
I was a happy man.

242
00:16:16,330 --> 00:16:17,750
I went through rich scenes.

243
00:16:18,029 --> 00:16:21,870
Oh, my experience has been heavenly if you only knew it.

244
00:16:23,089 --> 00:16:25,949
But I owe you no further explanation.

245
00:16:26,970 --> 00:16:31,457
Briggs, would, Mason, I invite you all to come up to the house and visit Mrs.

246
00:16:31,457 --> 00:16:33,470
Paul's patient and my wife.

247
00:16:34,169 --> 00:16:37,790
You shall see what sort of a being I was cheated into espousing.

248
00:16:38,790 --> 00:16:42,368
And judge whether or not I had a right to break the

249
00:16:42,368 --> 00:16:45,970
compact and seek sympathy with something at least human.

250
00:16:47,589 --> 00:16:51,716
This girl, he continued, looking at me, knew no

251
00:16:51,716 --> 00:16:55,230
more than you would of the disgusting secret.

252
00:16:56,129 --> 00:17:00,709
She thought all was fair and legal, and never dreamt she was going to be

253
00:17:00,711 --> 00:17:06,430
entrapped into a fained union with a defrauded wretch, already bound to a bad,

254
00:17:06,589 --> 00:17:08,230
mad, and imbruted partner.

255
00:17:08,949 --> 00:17:10,349
Come, all of you, follow.

256
00:17:11,430 --> 00:17:14,250
Still holding me fast, he left the church.

257
00:17:15,069 --> 00:17:16,529
The three gentlemen came after.

258
00:17:17,349 --> 00:17:20,029
At the front door of the hall, we found the carriage.

259
00:17:21,230 --> 00:17:25,110
Take it back to the coach house, John, said Mr. Rochester Cooley.

260
00:17:25,849 --> 00:17:27,389
It will not be wanted today.

261
00:17:28,410 --> 00:17:34,631
At our entrance, Mrs. Fairfax, Adele, Sophie, Leah, advanced to meet and greet us.

262
00:17:35,029 --> 00:17:39,669
To the right about every soul, cried the master, away with your

263
00:17:39,671 --> 00:17:44,569
congratulations, who wants them, not I, they are 15 years too late.

264
00:17:45,809 --> 00:17:51,650
He passed on and ascended the stairs, still holding my hand, and still beckoning

265
00:17:51,650 --> 00:17:54,129
the gentleman to follow him, which they did.

266
00:17:55,069 --> 00:18:01,071
We mounted the first staircase, passed up the gallery, preceded to the third story.

267
00:18:02,129 --> 00:18:07,790
The low black door, opened by Mr. Rochester's master key, admitted us to the

268
00:18:07,790 --> 00:18:12,150
tapestry room, with its great bed and its pictorial cabinet.

269
00:18:13,209 --> 00:18:15,989
You know this place, Mason, said our guide.

270
00:18:16,669 --> 00:18:18,069
She bit and stabbed you here.

271
00:18:18,809 --> 00:18:23,209
He lifted the hangings from the wall, uncovering the second door.

272
00:18:23,989 --> 00:18:25,430
This, too, he opened.

273
00:18:26,610 --> 00:18:31,849
In a room without a window, their burnt a fire guarded by a high and strong fender,

274
00:18:32,489 --> 00:18:35,150
and a lamp suspended from the ceiling by a chain.

275
00:18:36,430 --> 00:18:41,671
Grace pool bent over the fire, apparently cooking something in a saucepan.

276
00:18:41,790 --> 00:18:44,627
In the deep shade, at the farther end of the

277
00:18:44,629 --> 00:18:47,930
room, a figure ran backwards and forwards.

278
00:18:48,050 --> 00:18:54,650
What it was, where the beast or human being, one could not, at first sight, tell.

279
00:18:54,870 --> 00:18:57,870
It groveled, seemingly on all fours.

280
00:18:58,510 --> 00:19:03,330
It snatched and growled like some strange wild animal, but it was covered with

281
00:19:03,330 --> 00:19:08,169
clothing, and a quantity of dark, grizzled hair, wild as a main,

282
00:19:08,889 --> 00:19:10,129
hid its head and face.

283
00:19:11,529 --> 00:19:15,150
Good morning, Mrs. Pool, said Mr. Rochester.

284
00:19:15,830 --> 00:19:18,529
How are you, and how's your charge today?

285
00:19:20,069 --> 00:19:21,250
We're tolerable, sir.

286
00:19:21,769 --> 00:19:26,970
I thank you," replied Grace, lifting the boiling mess carefully onto the hob,

287
00:19:27,830 --> 00:19:30,230
rather snappish, but not rages.

288
00:19:31,010 --> 00:19:34,870
A fierce cry seemed to give the lie to her favorable report.

289
00:19:35,589 --> 00:19:39,650
The clothed hyena rose up and stood tall on its hind feet.

290
00:19:40,290 --> 00:19:42,970
Ah, sir, she sees you.

291
00:19:43,750 --> 00:19:44,750
Exclaimed Grace.

292
00:19:45,290 --> 00:19:46,290
You'd better not stay.

293
00:19:47,110 --> 00:19:50,290
Only a few moments Grace, you must allow me a few moments.

294
00:19:51,349 --> 00:19:52,349
Take care then, sir.

295
00:19:52,989 --> 00:19:54,290
For God's sake, take care.

296
00:19:55,309 --> 00:19:56,629
The maniac bellowed.

297
00:19:57,269 --> 00:20:02,529
She parted her shaggy locks from her visage and gazed wildly at her visitors.

298
00:20:02,531 --> 00:20:05,870
I recognized well that purple face.

299
00:20:06,709 --> 00:20:08,389
Those bloated features.

300
00:20:09,129 --> 00:20:10,709
Mrs. Pool advanced.

301
00:20:11,730 --> 00:20:15,269
Keep out of the way, said Mr. Rochester, thrusting her aside.

302
00:20:15,970 --> 00:20:18,769
She has no knife now, I suppose, and I'm on my guard.

303
00:20:20,010 --> 00:20:21,830
One never knows what she has, sir.

304
00:20:22,550 --> 00:20:27,250
She is so cunning, it is not in mortal discretion to fathom her craft.

305
00:20:28,709 --> 00:20:31,349
We had better leave her, whispered Mason.

306
00:20:32,529 --> 00:20:33,529
Go to the devil.

307
00:20:34,150 --> 00:20:36,129
Was his brother-in-law's recommendation.

308
00:20:37,389 --> 00:20:39,069
Where, cried Grace?

309
00:20:40,389 --> 00:20:42,790
The three gentlemen retreated simultaneously.

310
00:20:44,290 --> 00:20:46,330
Mr. Rochester flung me behind him.

311
00:20:47,169 --> 00:20:52,190
The lunatic sprang and grappled his throat viciously and laid her teeth to his cheek.

312
00:20:52,730 --> 00:20:53,730
They struggled.

313
00:20:53,870 --> 00:20:55,330
She was a big woman.

314
00:20:56,010 --> 00:21:00,275
In stature almost equalling her husband and corpulant

315
00:21:00,275 --> 00:21:03,470
besides, she showed virile force in the contest.

316
00:21:04,510 --> 00:21:08,430
More than once she almost throttled him, athletic as he was.

317
00:21:09,389 --> 00:21:13,650
He could have settled her with a well -planted blow, but he would not strike.

318
00:21:14,470 --> 00:21:15,569
He would only wrestle.

319
00:21:16,650 --> 00:21:19,230
At last, he mastered her arms.

320
00:21:20,330 --> 00:21:24,209
Grace Pool gave him a cord and he pinioned them behind her.

321
00:21:24,900 --> 00:21:28,809
With more rope, which was at hand, he bound her to a chair.

322
00:21:30,029 --> 00:21:35,451
The operation was performed amidst the fiercest yells in the most convulsive plunges.

323
00:21:36,529 --> 00:21:38,629
Mr. Rochester then turned to the spectators.

324
00:21:39,330 --> 00:21:42,370
He looked at them with a smile both accurate and desolate.

325
00:21:43,529 --> 00:21:45,709
That is my wife, said he.

326
00:21:46,529 --> 00:21:49,230
Such is the soul conjugal embrace I am ever to know.

327
00:21:50,069 --> 00:21:53,580
Such are the demons which are to solace my leisure hours.

328
00:21:54,220 --> 00:21:57,220
And this is what I wished to have.

329
00:21:58,919 --> 00:22:05,360
Laying his hand on my shoulder, this young girl, who stands so grave and

330
00:22:05,360 --> 00:22:09,660
quiet at the mouth of hell, looking collectively at the gambles of a demon,

331
00:22:10,540 --> 00:22:14,000
I wanted her just as a change after that fierce ragu.

332
00:22:14,839 --> 00:22:17,099
Wooden Briggs, look at the difference.

333
00:22:18,000 --> 00:22:23,900
Compare these clear eyes with the red balls yonder, this face with that mask,

334
00:22:24,639 --> 00:22:25,959
this form with that bulk.

335
00:22:27,099 --> 00:22:32,040
Then judge me, priest of the gospel and man of the law, and remember with what

336
00:22:32,040 --> 00:22:35,639
judgment ye judge ye shall be judged, off with you now.

337
00:22:36,379 --> 00:22:37,839
I must shut up my prize.

338
00:22:39,400 --> 00:22:40,900
We all withdrew.

339
00:22:42,099 --> 00:22:46,819
Mr. Rochester stayed a moment behind us to give some further order to grace pool.

340
00:22:47,660 --> 00:22:50,580
The solicitor addressed me as he descended the stair.

341
00:22:52,220 --> 00:22:56,760
You, madam, said he, are cleared from all blame.

342
00:22:57,660 --> 00:23:04,419
Your uncle will be glad to hear it if, indeed, he should be still living when Mr.

343
00:23:04,540 --> 00:23:06,059
Mason returns to Madera.

344
00:23:07,419 --> 00:23:09,459
My uncle, what of him?

345
00:23:09,559 --> 00:23:10,559
Do you know him?

346
00:23:11,440 --> 00:23:12,440
Mr. Mason does.

347
00:23:13,839 --> 00:23:17,919
Mr. Ayer has been the funshell correspondent of his house for some years.

348
00:23:19,019 --> 00:23:24,559
When your uncle received your letter intimating, the contemplated union between

349
00:23:24,561 --> 00:23:30,639
yourself and Mr. Rochester, Mr. Mason, who was staying at Madera to recruit his

350
00:23:30,641 --> 00:23:34,440
health on his way back to Jamaica, happened to be with him.

351
00:23:35,959 --> 00:23:40,959
Mr. Ayer mentioned the intelligence, for he knew that my client here was

352
00:23:40,961 --> 00:23:43,519
acquainted with a gentleman of the name of Rochester.

353
00:23:44,879 --> 00:23:48,512
Mr. Mason, astonished and distressed as you may

354
00:23:48,512 --> 00:23:52,061
suppose, revealed the real state of matters.

355
00:23:53,440 --> 00:23:59,599
Your uncle, I am sorry to say, is now on a sick bed, from which,

356
00:24:00,040 --> 00:24:05,440
considering the nature of his disease, decline and the stage it has reached,

357
00:24:06,120 --> 00:24:07,980
it is unlikely he will ever rise.

358
00:24:09,059 --> 00:24:14,120
He could not then hasten to England himself, to extricate you from the snare

359
00:24:14,120 --> 00:24:18,186
into which you had fallen, but he implored Mr. Mason to

360
00:24:18,186 --> 00:24:21,699
lose no time in taking steps to prevent the false marriage.

361
00:24:22,620 --> 00:24:24,779
He referred him to me for assistance.

362
00:24:26,180 --> 00:24:32,839
I used all dispatch, and I am thankful I was not too late, as you, doubtless,

363
00:24:33,279 --> 00:24:34,279
must be also.

364
00:24:35,599 --> 00:24:40,800
Were I not morally certain that your uncle will be dead air you reach Madera,

365
00:24:41,400 --> 00:24:47,379
I would advise you to accompany Mr. Mason back, but as it is, I think you'd better

366
00:24:47,459 --> 00:24:55,459
remain in England till you can else to stay for.

367
00:24:56,360 --> 00:24:57,559
He inquired of Mr. Mason.

368
00:24:58,580 --> 00:25:02,040
No, no, let us be gone, was the anxious reply.

369
00:25:02,940 --> 00:25:05,968
And without waiting to take leave of Mr. Rochester,

370
00:25:05,970 --> 00:25:08,760
they made their exit at the hall door.

371
00:25:09,620 --> 00:25:13,533
The clergyman stayed to exchange a few sentences, either

372
00:25:13,533 --> 00:25:17,360
of admonition or reproof with his haughty parishioner.

373
00:25:18,080 --> 00:25:20,699
This duty done, he too departed.

374
00:25:22,019 --> 00:25:26,097
I heard him go, as I stood at the half -open door

375
00:25:26,099 --> 00:25:29,521
of my own room, to which I had now withdrawn.

376
00:25:30,720 --> 00:25:36,819
The house cleared, I shut myself in, fastened the bolt that none might intrude

377
00:25:36,821 --> 00:25:44,319
and proceeded, not to weep, not to mourn, I was yet too calm for that, mechanically

378
00:25:44,321 --> 00:25:48,760
to take off the wedding dress and replace it by the stuff gown I had worn yesterday,

379
00:25:49,239 --> 00:25:50,900
as I thought for the last time.

380
00:25:51,959 --> 00:25:52,959
I then sat down.

381
00:25:53,940 --> 00:25:55,699
I felt weak and tired.

382
00:25:56,839 --> 00:26:02,459
I leaned my arms on a table and my head dropped on them, and now I thought,

383
00:26:03,160 --> 00:26:08,900
till now I had only heard scene moved, followed up and down where I was led or

384
00:26:08,900 --> 00:26:14,559
dragged, watched event, rush on event, disclosure opened beyond disclosure,

385
00:26:15,080 --> 00:26:16,779
but now I thought.

386
00:26:17,559 --> 00:26:20,375
The morning had been a quiet morning enough,

387
00:26:20,375 --> 00:26:23,480
all except the brief scene with the lunatic.

388
00:26:24,019 --> 00:26:26,440
The transaction in the church had not been noisy.

389
00:26:27,419 --> 00:26:32,919
There was no explosion of passion, no loud altercation, no dispute,

390
00:26:33,680 --> 00:26:37,260
no defiance or challenge, no tears, no sobs.

391
00:26:38,080 --> 00:26:42,900
A few words had been spoken, a calmly pronounced objection to the marriage made,

392
00:26:43,900 --> 00:26:50,180
some stern, short questions put by Mr. Rochester, answers, explanations given,

393
00:26:50,900 --> 00:26:55,860
evidence-adduced, an open admission of the truth had been uttered by my master.

394
00:26:56,680 --> 00:27:02,559
Then the living proof had been seen, the intruders were gone, and all was over.

395
00:27:03,519 --> 00:27:08,720
I was in my own room as usual, just myself, without obvious change.

396
00:27:09,599 --> 00:27:13,442
Nothing had smitten me, or scathed me, or maimed

397
00:27:13,442 --> 00:27:16,720
me, and yet, where was the Jane Eyre of yesterday?

398
00:27:17,300 --> 00:27:18,300
Where was her life?

399
00:27:18,720 --> 00:27:19,720
Where were her prospects?

400
00:27:20,599 --> 00:27:25,019
Jane Eyre, who had been an ardent, expectant woman almost a bride,

401
00:27:25,500 --> 00:27:27,620
was a cold solitary girl again.

402
00:27:28,400 --> 00:27:31,739
Her life was pale, her prospects were desolate.

403
00:27:33,419 --> 00:27:39,341
A Christmas frost had come at mid-summer, a white December storm had whirled over June.

404
00:27:39,580 --> 00:27:45,800
Ice glazed the ripe apples, drifts crushed the blowing roses, on hayfield and

405
00:27:45,800 --> 00:27:51,980
cornfield lay a frozen shroud, lanes which last night blushed full of flowers.

406
00:27:52,459 --> 00:27:59,459
Today were pathless with untrodden snow, and the woods, which 12 hours since waved

407
00:27:59,461 --> 00:28:05,139
leafy and fragrant as groves between the tropics, now spread, waste, wild,

408
00:28:05,260 --> 00:28:07,620
and white as pine forests in wintry Norway.

409
00:28:08,860 --> 00:28:14,313
My hopes were all dead, struck with a subtle doom, such as

410
00:28:14,315 --> 00:28:17,580
in one night fell on all the firstborn in the land of Egypt.

411
00:28:18,440 --> 00:28:22,779
I looked on my cherished wishes, yesterday so blooming and glowing,

412
00:28:23,500 --> 00:28:27,900
they lay stark, chill, livid corpses that could never revive.

413
00:28:28,819 --> 00:28:35,000
I looked at my love, that feeling which was my masters, which he had created.

414
00:28:35,720 --> 00:28:39,800
It shivered in my heart, like a suffering child in a cold cradle.

415
00:28:40,800 --> 00:28:43,019
Sickness and anguish had seized it.

416
00:28:43,639 --> 00:28:45,959
It could not seek Mr. Rochester's arms.

417
00:28:46,639 --> 00:28:48,680
It could not derive warmth from his breast.

418
00:28:49,860 --> 00:28:52,000
Oh, never more could it turn to him.

419
00:28:52,839 --> 00:28:54,419
For faith was blighted.

420
00:28:55,080 --> 00:28:56,500
Confidence destroyed.

421
00:28:57,959 --> 00:29:03,199
Mr. Rochester was not to me what he had been, for he was not what I had thought him.

422
00:29:03,849 --> 00:29:05,739
I would not ascribe vice to him.

423
00:29:06,680 --> 00:29:11,800
I would not say he had betrayed me, but the attribute of stainless truth was

424
00:29:11,800 --> 00:29:17,160
gone from his idea, and from his presence I must go, that I perceived well.

425
00:29:17,900 --> 00:29:24,599
When, how, wither, I could not yet discern, but he himself I doubted not,

426
00:29:25,199 --> 00:29:26,839
would hurry me from thornfield.

427
00:29:27,660 --> 00:29:30,139
Real affection it seemed he could not have for me.

428
00:29:30,919 --> 00:29:32,760
It had been only fitful passion.

429
00:29:33,379 --> 00:29:34,379
That was balked.

430
00:29:34,720 --> 00:29:35,800
He would want me no more.

431
00:29:37,300 --> 00:29:39,500
I should fear even to cross his path now.

432
00:29:40,279 --> 00:29:41,980
My view must be hateful to him.

433
00:29:42,860 --> 00:29:45,620
Oh, how blind had been my eyes, how weak my conduct.

434
00:29:46,319 --> 00:29:48,040
My eyes were covered and closed.

435
00:29:49,059 --> 00:29:52,059
Eddying darkness seemed to swim around me, and

436
00:29:52,061 --> 00:29:55,360
reflection came in as black and confused a flow.

437
00:29:56,580 --> 00:29:59,120
Self-abandoned, relaxed and effortless.

438
00:29:59,839 --> 00:30:03,080
I seemed to have laid me down in the dried up bed of a great river.

439
00:30:03,760 --> 00:30:08,540
I heard a flood loosened in remote mountains, and felt the torrent come.

440
00:30:09,500 --> 00:30:10,959
To rise I had no will.

441
00:30:11,639 --> 00:30:13,199
To flee I had no strength.

442
00:30:14,180 --> 00:30:16,779
I lay faint, longing to be dead.

443
00:30:17,959 --> 00:30:21,220
One idea only still throbbed life like within me.

444
00:30:21,839 --> 00:30:23,000
A remembrance of God.

445
00:30:23,779 --> 00:30:25,540
It begot an unuttered prayer.

446
00:30:26,160 --> 00:30:31,160
These words went wandering up and down in my railous mind, a something that should

447
00:30:31,161 --> 00:30:34,980
be whispered, but no energy was found to express them.

448
00:30:36,360 --> 00:30:37,519
Be not far from me.

449
00:30:38,260 --> 00:30:39,260
For trouble is near.

450
00:30:40,019 --> 00:30:41,279
There is none to help.

451
00:30:42,360 --> 00:30:46,739
It was near, and as I had lifted no petition to heaven to avert it,

452
00:30:47,180 --> 00:30:51,339
as I had neither joined my hands nor bent my knees nor moved my lips.

453
00:30:52,139 --> 00:30:53,139
It came.

454
00:30:53,680 --> 00:30:58,300
In full heavy swing the torrent poured over me, the whole consciousness of my

455
00:30:58,300 --> 00:31:03,419
life -lawn, my love-lost, my hope -quenched, my faith-death-struck,

456
00:31:04,199 --> 00:31:07,379
swayed full and mighty above me in one's sullen mass.

457
00:31:08,360 --> 00:31:10,860
That bitter hour cannot be described.

458
00:31:11,500 --> 00:31:14,839
In truth, the waters came into my soul.

459
00:31:15,779 --> 00:31:17,559
I sank in deep mire.

460
00:31:17,739 --> 00:31:19,160
I felt no standing.

461
00:31:19,919 --> 00:31:21,319
I came into deep waters.

462
00:31:22,260 --> 00:31:23,800
The floods overflowed me.

463
00:31:26,559 --> 00:31:33,160
Chapter 27 Sometime in the afternoon I raised my head, and looking round and

464
00:31:33,161 --> 00:31:38,300
seeing the western sun gilding the sign of its decline on the wall, I asked,

465
00:31:38,660 --> 00:31:40,160
what am I to do?

466
00:31:40,980 --> 00:31:47,019
But the answer my mind gave, leave Thornfield at once, was so prompt,

467
00:31:47,500 --> 00:31:49,419
so dread, that I stopped my ears.

468
00:31:50,059 --> 00:31:51,760
I said I could not bear such words now.

469
00:31:53,040 --> 00:31:59,199
That I am not Edward Rochester's bride is the least part of my woe, I alleged,

470
00:31:59,879 --> 00:32:03,862
that I have wakened out of most glorious dreams, and found

471
00:32:03,862 --> 00:32:07,940
them all void and vain is a horror I could bear and master.

472
00:32:08,860 --> 00:32:14,319
But that I must leave him decidedly, instantly, entirely, is intolerable.

473
00:32:14,819 --> 00:32:15,819
I cannot do it.

474
00:32:16,319 --> 00:32:19,142
But then, a voice within me, a bird that I

475
00:32:19,144 --> 00:32:23,641
could do it, and foretold that I should do it.

476
00:32:23,940 --> 00:32:25,000
I wrestled with my own resolution.
